      "writtenOn": "2025-11-20T17:32:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We enable device TLB even if the host didn\u0027t ask us to?\n\n...I think we should just always set CONTEXT_TT_MULTI_LEVEL. Even if we cared about supporting SATC on platforms that use legacy mode, see this comment in dmar_ats_supported():\n\n```\n\tsatcu \u003d dmar_find_matched_satc_unit(dev);\n\tif (satcu)\n\t\t/*\n\t\t * This device supports ATS as it is in SATC table.\n\t\t * When IOMMU is in legacy mode, enabling ATS is done\n\t\t * automatically by HW for the device that requires\n\t\t * ATS, hence OS should not enable this device ATS\n\t\t * to avoid duplicated TLB invalidation.\n\t\t */\n\t\treturn !(satcu-\u003eatc_required \u0026\u0026 !sm_supported(iommu));\n```",
      "revId": "c7ec47177158bdc7e2f56e23dc9f5ca6c8b2d929",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
