      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-21T17:33:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e We enable device TLB even if the host didn\u0027t ask us to?\n\nI was minimally mimicking the host driver (`domain_context_mapping_one`), but it was not complete as info-\u003eats_supported is derived from more factors than just presence in satc.\n\n\u003e ...I think we should just always set CONTEXT_TT_MULTI_LEVEL. Even if we cared about supporting SATC on platforms that use legacy mode, see this comment in dmar_ats_supported():\n\nMakes sense. I was mimicking the host driver as mentioned above, but info-\u003eats_supported is derived a bit complicated fashion and not worth porting to pkvm. So I have modified as you suggested.",
